        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Most students search for a 12th cut off calculator expecting a single formula. In reality, each state counselling authority defines its own calculation. The four worked examples below take the identical three marks &mdash;
          <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900">88 in Mathematics, 76 in Physics, and 81 in Chemistry</strong> &mdash;
          through four published state formulas so you can clearly see where each number originates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!--
        One column on every breakpoint. Prose keeps a comfortable ~68-character
        measure; the arithmetic sits in a full-width dashed strip below it, so
        nothing is ever pinched beside a narrow aside on a wide screen.
      -->
      {WORKED_EXAMPLES.map((ex, i) => (
        <article class="mt-12">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            <span class="font-mono text-slate-400">{i + 1}.</span> {ex.exam}
