            {ex.body.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
          </div>

          <p class="dashed-callout mt-4 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            {ex.equation} = <strong class="text-slate-900">{ex.result}</strong>
          </p>

          <!--
            Arithmetic strip.

            Flex-wrap, not a fixed `grid-cols-4`: KEAM has four line items and the
            other three exams have three, so a fixed 4-column grid left a bare
            grey cell in the corner of every non-KEAM example. With wrap and a
            percentage basis the cells simply fill whatever space they need and
            there is never an empty slot to render.

            The merit score is a separate full-width bar rather than a fifth
            cell: it is the answer the whole section exists to produce, so it
            gets the emphasis instead of being one item among four.
