            <span class="font-sans text-[0.75rem] uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Merit score</span>
            <strong class="text-base text-slate-900">{ex.result}</strong>
          </p>

          <!--
            `.note-card`, not the grey paragraph this used to be. `ex.note` is the
            catch-the-caveat line under each example — the eligibility gate, the
            capping, the arithmetic check — and as body-coloured prose at 14px it
            was the easiest thing in the section to scroll straight past, even
            though it is the part that stops someone entering the wrong number.
            A panel with an icon and a "Note" label is read as a note; a lighter
            grey paragraph is not.

            The title is visible text inside the panel, so the aside needs no
            `aria-label` of its own: a label duplicating that string would make a
            screen reader announce "Note, Note" before the sentence.
